g-sur-les-lignes-asm/","title":"La version 1.93 du langage de programmation Rust est disponible, introduisant musl 1.2.5, des améliorations de l'allocateur et des attributs cfg sur les lignes asm!","snippet":"Rust 1.93 est désormais disponible, avec des mises à jour qui concernent à la fois les développeurs et l'écosystème Rust au sens large. Dans cette version, toutes les cibles *-linux-musl sont livrées ","site_name":"Developpez.com","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/developpez.com","published_at":"2026-01-25T16:00:00+00:00"},{"type":"url","url":"https://www.developpez.net/forums/i2181709/general-developpement/programmation-systeme/rust/rust-1-93-apporte-musl-1-2-5-ameliorations-lallocateur-attributs-cfg-lignes-asm/#1","title":"Rust 1.93 apporte musl 1.2.5, des améliorations de l'allocateur et des attributs cfg sur les lignes asm! - - 25/01/2026, 04h52 Alex Rust 1.93 apporte musl 1.2.5, des améliorations de l'allocateur et des attributs cfg sur les lignes asm","snippet":"- 25/01/2026, 04h52 Alex Rust 1.93 apporte musl 1.2.5, des améliorations de l'allocateur et des attributs cfg sur les lignes asm!La version 1.93 du langage de programmation Rust est disponible, introd","site_name":"Developpez.net","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/developpez.net","published_at":"2026-01-24T16:00:00+00:00"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/tags/release/","title":"Posts tagged \"release\" | Rust Blog","snippet":"Posts in 2026 ... 5 | Announcing Rust 1.94.0 Feb. 12 | Announcing Rust 1.93.1 Jan. 22 | Announcing Rust 1.93.0 ## Posts in 2025","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/?source=post_page-----a11ed1e7fcd2--------------------------------","title":"The Rust Programming Language Blog","snippet":"development update ... Feb. 12 | Announcing Rust 1.93.1 Jan. 22 | Announcing Rust 1.93.0 Jan. 21 | crates.io: development update Jan.","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/inside-rust/2026/01/07/this-development-cycle-in-cargo-1.93/?ref=dailydev#implementation","title":"This Development-cycle in Cargo: 1.93 | Inside Rust Blog","snippet":"This Development-cycle in Cargo: 1.93 Jan. 7, 2026 ... This is a summary of what has been happening around Cargo development for the last 6 weeks which is approximately the merge window for Rust 1.93. ... Update from 1.92","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org","published_at":"2026-01-06T16:00:00+00:00"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/12/05/Updating-musl-1.2.5/#tier-2-with-host-tools","title":"Updating Rust's Linux musl targets to 1.2.5 | Rust Blog","snippet":"Beginning with Rust 1.93 (slated for stable release on 2026-01-22), the various*-linux-musl targets will all ship with musl 1.2.5. This primarily affects static musl builds for x86_64, aarch64, and po","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org","published_at":"2026-01-21T16:00:00+00:00"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/inside-rust/?utm_source=cosmicmeta&utm_medium=u2m.io","title":"The \"Inside Rust\" Blog","snippet":"### Posts in 2026  Apr. 6 | Leadership Council update — March 2026  Mar. 27 | Program management update — February 2026  Mar. 25 | January & February 2026 Project Director Update  Feb. 18 | This Devel","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/12/19/what-do-people-love-about-rust/?via=dailydev#but-the-balance-is-crucial","title":"What do people love about Rust? | Rust Blog","snippet":"Dec. 19, 2025 · Niko Matsakis on behalf of Vision Doc group  Rust has been named Stack Overflow's Most Loved (now called Most Admired) language every year since our 1.0 release in 2015. That means peo","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org","published_at":"2025-12-18T16:00:00+00:00"},{"type":"url","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2021/05/15/six-years-of-rust/","title":"Six Years of Rust | Rust Blog","snippet":"May 15, 2021 · The Rust Team  Today marks Rust's sixth birthday since it went 1.0 in 2015. A lot has changed since then and especially over the past year, and Rust was no different. In 2020, there was","site_name":"Rust Language Blog","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org","published_at":"2021-05-14T16:00:00+00:00"}]}},"output_index":5,"sequence_number":264}

