ek.com/site-icons/rust-lang.org","published_at":"2021-05-14T16:00:00+00:00"}]}},{"type":"reasoning","id":"7e658241-9987-4fa2-b496-1c2de79b7b60","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"Interesting! Official blog release page shows releases in 2026 up to Oct 15, 2026: Rust 1.99.1. The search index appears to reflect a date after Oct 15, 2026. So latest stable is Rust 1.99.1, released October 15, 2026.\n\nWait, but is 1.99.1 the latest stable? Release list says Oct. 15 | Announcing Rust 1.99.1. So yes. Could there be a newer release after Oct 15 2026 not indexed? Current context may be around late 2026. Search results only up to Oct 15, 2026. Need to confirm whether 1.99.1 is stable and latest, perhaps 1.100 isn't released yet. Let me open the latest release post to confirm date and version. Also maybe the /releases/latest redirect."}],"summary":[]},{"type":"web_search_call","id":"srvtoolu_ds_04_af5d52622b32473f940a66c87e8e193f","status":"completed","kind":"deep_search","action":{"type":"open_page","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/15/Rust-1.99.1/"},"page":{"url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/15/Rust-1.99.1/","title":"Announcing Rust 1.99.1 | Rust Blog","published_at":null}},{"type":"web_search_call","id":"srvtoolu_ds_05_f7cc2950c1724853b60f0b242bccf41a","status":"failed","kind":"deep_search","action":{"type":"open_page","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/latest"},"error":{"code":"unavailable"}},{"type":"reasoning","id":"fb7e619e-1c6b-40d2-80df-32849b2a8c45","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"Confirmed: Rust 1.99.1, October 15, 2026. But wait—1.99.1 is a point release; \"latest stable version\" is 1.99.1. Release date Oct 15, 2026.\n\nNeed answer in one sentence with citation. Cite official blog lines. Could mention \"Rust 1.99.1, released October 15, 2026\" with citation . Maybe also release page . One sentence only.\n\nCheck if 1.99.1 stable vs maybe beta? Blog says point release, rustup upd